{%- comment -%}
  One saved product for the Saved page (docs/account-plan.md §8.3). Never placed on a page: saved-page.js asks for it
  with the Section Rendering API on the product's own URL (/products/<handle>?section_id=saved-item), so the card
  always shows today's price and stock.
  Under the card: Add to cart (one-option products, via cart.js and its pop-up), Choose options, or for sold-out
  pieces "Ask us to make one".
  The cart's Saved for later and Recently viewed rows use it too (assets/cart-rows.js).
  The free gift and test products (tag "test-product") give nothing back, so a piece saved or seen before it was
  taken off sale drops out of every list: the Saved page reads the empty answer as "no longer available".
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- render 'saved-card', product: product -%}

{% stylesheet %}
  .saved-item { display: grid; grid-template-rows: 1fr auto; gap: var(--space-3); min-width: 0; }
  .saved-item__btn { width: 100%; min-height: var(--tap); padding-inline: var(--space-3); font-size: .9375rem; white-space: normal; text-align: center; }
  .saved-item__form { display: block; }
  /* Removing: the card folds away, then the grid closes the gap. */
  .saved-item.is-leaving { opacity: 0; scale: .96; transition: opacity 220ms var(--ease-exit), scale 220ms var(--ease-exit); }
  /* In Recently viewed, just the cards. */
  .saved__recent .saved-item__actions { display: none; }
{% endstylesheet %}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Saved item",
  "settings": []
}
{% endschema %}
